stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> GateRequired : new browser session<br/>readAiSession() === null
    GateRequired --> Preparing : ai.setPreparing() (in-memory only,<br/>not persisted to sessionStorage)
    Preparing --> Ready : backend state=ready AND can_continue_with_ai<br/>markAiReady(modelId) written to sessionStorage
    Preparing --> Unavailable : backend blocked/failed/backend_unavailable<br/>(transient, in-memory only)
    Unavailable --> Preparing : user retries (Settings or onboarding gate)
    Unavailable --> NonAi : user clicks "Continue without AI"<br/>markNonAi() written to sessionStorage
    GateRequired --> NonAi : user clicks "Continue without AI" directly
    Ready --> Preparing : user retries in Settings (switch model)
    NonAi --> Preparing : user opens the gate again from Settings notice
    Ready --> [*] : signOutCompletely() → clearAiSession()
    NonAi --> [*] : signOutCompletely() → clearAiSession()
    GateRequired --> [*] : signOutCompletely() → clearAiSession() (no-op, already null)

    note right of Ready
      Persisted key: sessionStorage "alim.ai_session.v1"
      { mode: "ai-ready", modelId, decidedAt }
      Survives client-side navigation, cleared on
      real sign-out and on browser/tab session end.
    end note
    note right of NonAi
      { mode: "non-ai", modelId: null, decidedAt }
      AI-dependent UI renders AiUnavailableNotice
      instead of fabricating a response.
    end note
